(1,1);\nD=(0,1);\nE=(0.3,1.5);\nF=C+(E-D);\nG=B+(E-D);\nH=A+(E-D);\n\ndraw(A--B--C--D--A--H--E);\ndraw(D--C--F);\ndraw(H--G);\ndraw(D--E--F--G--B);\n\ndot(A);\ndot(B);\ndot(C);\ndot(D);\ndot(E);\ndot(F);\ndot(G);\ndot(H);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"adb43f80a20eed354af209e92fdfa8cbdc4adff78d0a1df12cf5d6320be61b25"},"seconds":8.489804983139038,"seed":874932341029832769,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by expressing the surface area and the volume of the cube in terms of its edge length \\( s \\).\n\nThe surface area of the cube is given by:\n\\[ 6s^2 \\]\n\nThe volume of the cube is given by:\n\\[ s^3 \\]\n\nAccording to the problem, the surface area is equal to the sum of the volume and five times the edge length. This can be written as:\n\\[ 6s^2 = s^3 + 5s \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( s \\), we rearrange the equation:\n\\[ s^3 - 6s^2 + 5s = 0 \\]\n\nWe can factor out \\( s \\) from the equation:\n\\[ s(s^2 - 6s + 5) = 0 \\]\n\nThis gives us one solution immediately:\n\\[ s = 0 \\]\n\nHowever, the problem states that \\( s > 0 \\), so \\( s = 0 \\) is not a valid solution. We now need to solve the quadratic equation:\n\\[ s^2 - 6s + 5 = 0 \\]\n\nWe can factorize the quadratic equation:\n\\[ (s - 1)(s - 5) = 0 \\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[ s = 1 \\]\n\\[ s = 5 \\]\n\nBoth solutions are positive, so they are both valid. The sum of all possible values of \\( s \\) is:\n\\[ 1 + 5 = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all possible values of \\( s \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:139"}
